# Ratio - fifty patches, six operators and thirty-two ways of wiring them.
#
# Each operator has sixteen waveforms, eight modes, a ratio from a quarter to
# sixty-four, its own feedback and its own four-stage envelope. On top of that
# are two algorithms at once with a morph between them, which no other machine
# here has, and snap and skew on the ratios. A bank of seven was a sample of
# it.
#
# The patches are grouped the way this kind of synthesis is actually heard -
# keys, bells and metal, basses, leads and brass, organs and reeds, strings
# and pads, then percussion and effects - rather than by algorithm, because
# nobody hears "algorithm fourteen" as a category. Spread through those groups
# are the ones that are this machine's own rather than the family's: the morph
# between two algorithms, the skew that fans the partials apart, and `snap`
# set to none so a ratio can sit between two notes of the scale.
#
# **Bells get their own demo.** A struck sound is its tail, and every other
# phrase here starts the next note before the last one has finished. `bell`
# leaves a second and a half between strikes, puts two together so two tails
# beat, and leaves the last one ringing on its own.
#
# Levelled to the house figure of -21 dB on the loudness column, the same as
# every other machine in the app. Five decibels of that came out of the
# machine's own output (`kHouse` in Ratio.cpp) so Init lands there too. Five
# patches sit one to six decibels under and all five are either a single
# operator with nothing modulating it or a strike short enough that four
# hundred milliseconds of it is mostly silence.
#
# **Three patches did not play the note you pressed**, which is the fault this
# kind of synthesis invites and the range sweep is the only thing that finds
# it: a carrier written at half the ratio sounded an octave down, one at four
# times sounded two octaves up, and one with the *carrier* fixed rather than
# the modulator sounded fifty hertz whatever key was held. A ratio is a
# multiplier on the note, so the carrier's is almost always one and everything
# interesting happens in the operators feeding it.
#
# Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Ratio` lists
# them. A patch names only what it changes.

machine Ratio
role    keys

patch Init

